  "Question": "A football game was played between two teams, the Cougars and the Panthers. The two teams scored a total of \\(34\\) points, and the Cougars won by a margin of \\(14\\) points. How many points did the Panthers score?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(10\\)",
    "B": "\\(14\\)",
    "C": "\\(17\\)",
    "D": "\\(20\\)",
    "E": "\\(24\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The Cougars scored \\(14\\) more points than the Panthers. Subtracting those extra points from the combined total leaves two equal amounts, each equal to the Panthers' score. Therefore the Panthers scored\n\\[\n\\frac{34-14}{2}=\\frac{20}{2}=\\boxed{10}\n\\]\npoints, choice A.",
